[18.792,"o","\r\n============================================================\r\n   SAIL-PROXY Docker Setup\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\nThis script will help you configure the SAP LLM Gateway\r\nfor Docker deployment, including:\r\n  - Service environment files (.env)\r\n  - Authentication providers\r\n  - Security tokens and secrets\r\n\r\n🤖 Running in CI/CD mode - using default options\r\n   - Local Development authentication\r\n   - No backup creation\r\n   - Localhost deployment\r\n\r\n⚠️  Running in FORCE mode - existing .env files will be overwritten!\r\n\r\n\r\nChecking service configuration files...\r\n\r\n📝 Creating Gateway .env file...\r\n\r\nSAP AI Core Configuration\r\n========================\r\n\r\n✅ Found SAP AI Core service key in environment variable SAP_AI_CORE_SERVICE_KEY\r\nExtracted configuration:\r\n  - SAP AI Core URL: https://api.ai.example.sap/v2\r\n  - Auth URL: https://auth.example.sap/oauth/token\r\n  - Region: eu10\r\n\r\n🚀 Using SAP AI Core service key from environment variable\r\n   Skipping interactive configuration...\r\n\r\n✅ Gateway .env created successfully\r\n📝 Creating Admin .env file...\r\n✅ Admin .env created successfully\r\n📝 Creating Ollama .env file...\r\n✅ Ollama .env created successfully\r\n\r\n🔐 Validating shared security tokens...\r\n\r\n✅ VALIDATION_TOKEN_SECRET matches\r\n✅ METADATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY matches\r\n\r\n✅ All security tokens validated successfully\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\n   Authentication Provider Setup\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n🤖 CI Mode: Auto-selecting Local Development provider\r\n\r\n🤖 CI Mode: Existing configuration files detected - skipping backup\r\n\r\n🤖 CI Mode: Using default configuration for Local Development (hardcoded users)\r\n\r\n🤖 CI Mode: Using localhost for development\r\n\r\n🤖 CI Mode: Using local builds for Docker images\r\n\r\n\r\nConfiguring Docker image settings...\r\n✅ Created .env.docker with local mode configuration\r\n✅ Created docker-compose.override.yml for local builds\r\n\r\n✅ Created .env file for manual docker-compose commands\r\n\r\nCopying and configuring files...\r\n✅ Updated admin .env with ROLE_MAPPING\r\nℹ️  Nginx configuration is now handled via environment variables\r\n   See docker/nginx/README.md for details\r\n✅ .env.postgres configured\r\n✅ .env.filesearch-runtime configured\r\n✅ .env.nginx created with BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080\r\n✅ Database credentials written to docker/.env (POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD)\r\n✅ dex.config.yaml configured\r\n✅ .env.auth configured\r\n✅ Removed docker-compose.override.yml (not needed for this provider)\r\n✅ Created placeholder okta-saml-ca.pem file for Dex service\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\n   Setup Complete! 🎉\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n✅ Configured for: Local Development (hardcoded users)\r\n✅ Base URL: http://localhost:8080\r\n"]
[19.102,"o","\r\nGenerated/Updated files:\r\n  Service Configuration:\r\n  - services/gateway/.env (SAP AI Core configuration)\r\n  - services/admin/.env (Admin service configuration)\r\n  - services/ollama/.env (Ollama service configuration)\r\n  Authentication Configuration:\r\n  - .env.nginx (Nginx environment variables)\r\n  - dex.config.yaml (with provider-specific configuration)\r\n  - .env.auth (updated OAuth2 URLs)\r\n  - .env.postgres (PostgreSQL configuration for Docker)\r\n\r\n💡 Configuration verification:\r\n   node verify-config.js\r\n\r\n✅ Nginx uses environment variables for configuration!\r\n   No rebuild required - configuration is applied at container startup.\r\n   The nginx image can be built once and reused across environments.\r\n\r\n🍎 Apple Silicon (ARM64) Detected\r\n   All services support native ARM64 for optimal performance.\r\n\r\nNext steps:\r\n1. Build containers (only needed once):\r\n   docker-compose build\r\n\r\n   Note: Future configuration changes only require container restart.\r\n\r\n2. Start the services:\r\n   docker-compose up -d\r\n\r\n3. Access the application:\r\n   http://localhost:8080/admin/\r\n\r\n💡 Apple Silicon Notes:\r\n   • All images are now multi-architecture (ARM64 and AMD64)\r\n   • Native ARM64 performance for optimal speed\r\n   • No platform-specific overrides needed\r\n\r\n4. Test users:\r\n   - admin@example.com / admin123\r\n   - user@example.com / user123\r\n\r\n🔑 Generated Credentials:\r\n   Save these credentials for future access:\r\n\r\n   📊 Database Credentials:\r\n   - Username: admin_user\r\n   - Password: [User-provided password]\r\n\r\n   🔐 OAuth2 Proxy Secrets:\r\n   - Client Secret: ••••••••\r\n   - Cookie Secret: ••••••••\r\n\r\n   These credentials are stored in your .env files and used by the services.\r\n   The database password is randomized for security.\r\n\r\n🔒 Security Reminders:\r\n   - Review .env files for sensitive data before committing to git\r\n   - Use OS environment variables for production secrets\r\n   - Set restrictive file permissions: chmod 600 services/*/.env\r\n   - Consider external secret management for enterprise deployments\r\n\r\nFor troubleshooting, check the logs:\r\n   docker-compose logs\r\n\r\n$ "]
